<UserControl
    x:Class="ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Settings.AppearanceSettingsView"
    xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:automation="clr-namespace:Avalonia.Automation;assembly=Avalonia.Controls"
    xmlns:home="clr-namespace:ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Home"
    xmlns:player="clr-namespace:ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Player"
    xmlns:settings="clr-namespace:ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Settings"
    xmlns:theme="clr-namespace:ApSolutions.LocalMedia.Presentation.Theme"
    x:DataType="settings:AppearanceSettingsViewModel"
    automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccessibleName}">
  <UserControl.Resources>
    <home:ResourceKeyConverter x:Key="AppearanceResourceKey" />
    <!--
      The same converter the subtitle preview paints with: a string of six hexadecimal digits is a
      colour in exactly one way, and a second implementation of that is a second answer waiting to
      disagree. It falls back rather than throwing, which is what a swatch bound to a value somebody
      is still moving needs.
    -->
    <player:SubtitleColourConverter x:Key="AppearanceColour" />
  </UserControl.Resources>
  <Border Padding="32" Background="{DynamicResource ShellSurfaceBrush}">
    <StackPanel MaxWidth="620" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
      <TextBlock
          FontSize="{DynamicResource FontSizeSubtitle}"
          FontWeight="SemiBold"
          Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimaryBrush}"
          Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceTitle}"
          automation:AutomationProperties.HeadingLevel="2" />
      <TextBlock
          Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimaryBrush}"
          Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDescription}"
          TextWrapping="Wrap" />
      <!--
        The two row-cards of this page put their pills UNDER the name rather than against the right
        edge, and that is measured rather than conceded. A WrapPanel in an Auto column is measured
        with infinite width, so it lays every pill on one line and only re-wraps at arrange time -
        which is the infinite-width shape this repository has now caught nine times, and the one
        AppearanceSettingsTests exists to refuse around exactly these buttons. The prototype's own
        `seg` row wraps for the same reason: `flex-wrap: wrap` with a ceiling, not a fixed column.

        So the card is what changes and the geometry inside it is not: the pills keep a bounded width
        to wrap inside, which is what they had, and what they gain is the surface the rest of the page
        now has. The pills against the right edge is a separate change with a separate measurement.
      -->
      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceThemeLabel}" />
          <!--
            A WrapPanel and not a horizontal StackPanel. §4 gives the reason as "five will not fit in 620",
            and that reason is void: there are three, and measured on 2026-08-21 they total 263 px in
            Spanish and 241 in English inside a 620-wide column. What earns the change is the shape - a
            horizontal StackPanel offers its children infinite width and draws them where they fall, which
            is how a control has ended up outside the window eight times here - and the fact that the
            length of these labels belongs to a translator rather than to this file.

            Three and not five, and that is decided rather than pending: ThemePreference.cs says the two
            high-contrast variants are a state read from Windows, not a fourth and fifth choice to pick.
          -->
          <WrapPanel ItemSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}" LineSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource ThemeSystem}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyThemeCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:ThemePreference.System}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding SystemStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource ThemeSystem}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource ThemeLight}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyThemeCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:ThemePreference.Light}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding LightStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource ThemeLight}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource ThemeDark}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyThemeCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:ThemePreference.Dark}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding DarkStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource ThemeDark}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <!--
              The fourth and fifth pills, chosen rather than only inherited — the owner revoked the
              choosable-high-contrast refusal on 2026-08-23. The system's own high contrast still
              wins over whichever pill is on, and the WrapPanel decides where five fold: with the
              Spanish labels they break one way and with the English ones another, so no line is
              fixed by hand.
            -->
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource ThemeHighContrastLight}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyThemeCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:ThemePreference.HighContrastLight}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding HighContrastLightStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource ThemeHighContrastLight}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource ThemeHighContrastDark}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyThemeCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:ThemePreference.HighContrastDark}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding HighContrastDarkStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource ThemeHighContrastDark}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>
      <!--
        The nine rows the prototype offers beside the theme and the language, in its own order. Each
        one is a setting-row: the name and the sentence that says what it does on the left, the state
        and the control against the right edge, which is what that class exists for.
      -->
      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space4}">
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceFollowWindowsLabel}" />
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceFollowWindowsDescription}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel
              Grid.Column="1"
              Orientation="Horizontal"
              Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding FollowsWindowsTheme}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOn}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding !FollowsWindowsTheme}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOff}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <CheckBox
                x:Name="FollowWindowsThemeCheckBox"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                IsChecked="{Binding FollowsWindowsTheme}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceFollowWindowsLabel}" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <!--
        The accent, as the prototype draws it: six circular swatches and the value beside them in a
        fixed-width face. Each swatch carries the state glyph as well as its fill — in either high
        contrast dictionary the six fills resolve to the same colour, so the glyph is the whole
        signal there, which is the same reason every pill row in this tree carries one.

        The six hexadecimals are written here and in AccentPalette.Presets, and that is not two
        sources: the swatch has to paint the colour it stands for, and a Background bound through a
        converter would be a converter whose only job is to turn a string into the string beside it.
        AppearanceSwatchTests compares the two lists, so they cannot drift apart in silence.
      -->
      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentLabel}" />
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentDescription}" />
          <WrapPanel ItemSpacing="{DynamicResource Space8}" LineSpacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
            <Button
                x:Name="FirstAccentSwatch"
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsFirstAccent}"
                Background="#1769AA"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#1769AA"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#1769AA" />
            <Button
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsSecondAccent}"
                Background="#2D6A4F"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#2D6A4F"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#2D6A4F" />
            <Button
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsThirdAccent}"
                Background="#8E4B2E"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#8E4B2E"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#8E4B2E" />
            <Button
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsFourthAccent}"
                Background="#6B4E9B"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#6B4E9B"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#6B4E9B" />
            <Button
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsFifthAccent}"
                Background="#B23A48"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#B23A48"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#B23A48" />
            <Button
                Classes="accent-swatch"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsSixthAccent}"
                Background="#0E7490"
                Command="{Binding ApplyAccentCommand}"
                CommandParameter="#0E7490"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="#0E7490" />
            <!--
              The hairline the prototype puts between the presets and the picker: the six on the left
              are choices, and what is on the right is a way to any colour at all.
            -->
            <Border
                Width="1"
                Height="22"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Background="{DynamicResource ShellHairlineBrush}" />
            <!--
              The seventh circle is the picker, and it is the prototype's own «elige cualquier color».
              Its <input type=color> opens the browser's grid; this opens the same shape built out of
              controls this application already owns — a grid of hues and lightnesses, three sliders
              for anything between them, and the value in the fixed-width face the row already
              carries. It wears the colour in force, so a custom colour is visible on the row itself
              rather than only inside the flyout.
            -->
            <Button
                x:Name="CustomAccentSwatch"
                Classes="accent-swatch custom"
                Classes.selected="{Binding IsCustomAccent}"
                Background="{Binding AccentHex, Converter={StaticResource AppearanceColour}}"
                ToolTip.Tip="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentCustom}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentCustom}">
              <Path Classes="icon size-14" Data="{DynamicResource IconChevronDown}" Stroke="{DynamicResource AccentTextBrush}" />
              <Button.Flyout>
                <Flyout Placement="Bottom">
                  <StackPanel Width="304" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
                    <TextBlock
                        Classes="setting-name"
                        Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentCustom}" />
                    <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
                      <Ellipse
                          Width="44"
                          Height="44"
                          Stroke="{DynamicResource ShellBorderBrush}"
                          StrokeThickness="1"
                          Fill="{Binding AccentHex, Converter={StaticResource AppearanceColour}}" />
                      <TextBlock
                          Grid.Column="1"
                          VerticalAlignment="Center"
                          FontFamily="{DynamicResource FontFamilyMono}"
                          Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondaryBrush}"
                          Text="{Binding AccentHex}" />
                    </Grid>
                    <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Static settings:AppearanceSettingsViewModel.ColourGrid}">
                      <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                        <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                          <WrapPanel />
                        </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                      </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                      <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                        <DataTemplate x:DataType="x:String">
                          <Button
                              x:Name="AccentGridCell"
                              Classes="colour-cell"
                              Background="{Binding ., Converter={StaticResource AppearanceColour}}"
                              Command="{Binding $parent[settings:AppearanceSettingsView].((settings:AppearanceSettingsViewModel)DataContext).ApplyAccentCommand}"
                              CommandParameter="{Binding .}"
                              ToolTip.Tip="{Binding .}"
                              automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceColourCell}"
                              automation:AutomationProperties.HelpText="{Binding .}" />
                        </DataTemplate>
                      </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    </ItemsControl>
                    <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentHue}" />
                    <Slider
                        x:Name="AccentHueSlider"
                        Classes="hue"
                        Minimum="0"
                        Maximum="360"
                        TickFrequency="1"
                        IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
                        Value="{Binding AccentHue, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentHue}" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentSaturation}" />
                    <Slider
                        x:Name="AccentSaturationSlider"
                        Minimum="0"
                        Maximum="100"
                        TickFrequency="1"
                        IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
                        Value="{Binding AccentSaturation, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentSaturation}" />
                    <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentLightness}" />
                    <Slider
                        x:Name="AccentLightnessSlider"
                        Minimum="0"
                        Maximum="100"
                        TickFrequency="1"
                        IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
                        Value="{Binding AccentLightness, Mode=TwoWay}"
                        automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentLightness}" />
                    <TextBlock
                        Classes="setting-description"
                        Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAccentDerivedNote}"
                        TextWrapping="Wrap" />
                  </StackPanel>
                </Flyout>
              </Button.Flyout>
            </Button>
            <TextBlock
                x:Name="AccentHexReadout"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                FontFamily="{DynamicResource FontFamilyMono}"
                Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondaryBrush}"
                Text="{Binding AccentHex}" />
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space4}">
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceMicaLabel}" />
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceMicaDescription}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel
              Grid.Column="1"
              Orientation="Horizontal"
              Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding Mica}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOn}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding !Mica}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOff}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <CheckBox
                x:Name="MicaCheckBox"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                IsChecked="{Binding Mica}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceMicaLabel}" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceTintLabel}" />
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceTintDescription}" />
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Slider
                x:Name="AccentTintSlider"
                Grid.Column="0"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Minimum="0"
                Maximum="100"
                TickFrequency="5"
                IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
                Value="{Binding TintPercent, Mode=TwoWay}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceTintLabel}" />
            <TextBlock
                Grid.Column="1"
                Classes="setting-state"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Text="{Binding TintPercent, StringFormat={}{0:0} %}" />
          </Grid>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityLabel}" />
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityDescription}" />
          <WrapPanel ItemSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}" LineSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityCompact}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyDensityCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:InterfaceDensity.Compact}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding CompactCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityCompact}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityComfortable}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyDensityCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:InterfaceDensity.Comfortable}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding ComfortableCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityComfortable}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityRoomy}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyDensityCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:InterfaceDensity.Roomy}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding RoomyCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceDensityRoomy}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverSizeLabel}" />
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverSizeDescription}" />
          <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Slider
                x:Name="CoverSizeSlider"
                Grid.Column="0"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Minimum="{x:Static settings:AppearanceSettingsViewModel.MinimumCoverWidth}"
                Maximum="{x:Static settings:AppearanceSettingsViewModel.MaximumCoverWidth}"
                TickFrequency="2"
                IsSnapToTickEnabled="True"
                Value="{Binding CoverWidth, Mode=TwoWay}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverSizeLabel}" />
            <TextBlock
                Grid.Column="1"
                Classes="setting-state"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                Text="{Binding CoverWidth, StringFormat={}{0:0} px}" />
          </Grid>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingLabel}" />
          <WrapPanel ItemSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}" LineSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingSharp}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyRoundingCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:CornerRounding.Sharp}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding SharpCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingSharp}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingSoft}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyRoundingCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:CornerRounding.Soft}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding SoftCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingSoft}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingVeryRound}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyRoundingCommand}"
                CommandParameter="{x:Static theme:CornerRounding.VeryRound}">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding VeryRoundCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceRoundingVeryRound}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space4}">
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverTitlesLabel}" />
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverTitlesDescription}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel
              Grid.Column="1"
              Orientation="Horizontal"
              Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding CoverTitles}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOn}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding !CoverTitles}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOff}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <CheckBox
                x:Name="CoverTitlesCheckBox"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                IsChecked="{Binding CoverTitles}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceCoverTitlesLabel}" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space4}">
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAnimationsLabel}" />
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearanceAnimationsDescription}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel
              Grid.Column="1"
              Orientation="Horizontal"
              Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}"
              VerticalAlignment="Center">
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding Animations}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOn}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <TextBlock
                Classes="setting-state"
                IsVisible="{Binding !Animations}"
                Text="{DynamicResource SettingStateOff}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.AccessibilityView="Raw" />
            <CheckBox
                x:Name="AnimationsCheckBox"
                VerticalAlignment="Center"
                IsChecked="{Binding Animations}"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource AppearanceAnimationsLabel}" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <!--
        The one row with no control, which the prototype draws the same way: the player's surface is
        dark in all four themes because a light strip under a picture is a seam, and that is a
        decision rather than a preference. Written down so nobody looks for the switch.
      -->
      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="*,Auto" ColumnSpacing="{DynamicResource Space16}">
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="0" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space4}">
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-name" Text="{DynamicResource AppearancePlayerSurfaceLabel}" />
            <TextBlock Classes="setting-description" Text="{DynamicResource AppearancePlayerSurfaceDescription}" />
          </StackPanel>
          <TextBlock
              Grid.Column="1"
              Classes="setting-state"
              VerticalAlignment="Center"
              IsVisible="{Binding PlayerSurfaceIsFixed}"
              Text="{DynamicResource AppearancePlayerSurfaceValue}" />
        </Grid>
      </Border>

      <Border Classes="setting-row">
        <StackPanel Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
          <TextBlock
              Classes="setting-name"
              FontSize="{DynamicResource FontSizeBody}"
              Text="{DynamicResource LanguageTitle}"
              automation:AutomationProperties.HeadingLevel="3" />
          <TextBlock
              Classes="setting-description"
              Text="{DynamicResource LanguageDescription}" />
          <WrapPanel ItemSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}" LineSpacing="{DynamicResource Space12}">
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource LanguageSpanish}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyLanguageCommand}"
                CommandParameter="es">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding SpanishStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource LanguageSpanish}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
            <Button
                Classes="theme-option"
                automation:AutomationProperties.Name="{DynamicResource LanguageEnglish}"
                Command="{Binding ApplyLanguageCommand}"
                CommandParameter="en">
              <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="{DynamicResource Space8}">
                <TextBlock Classes="state-glyph" Text="{Binding EnglishStateCue}" />
                <TextBlock Text="{DynamicResource LanguageEnglish}" />
              </StackPanel>
            </Button>
          </WrapPanel>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>
      <!--
        Which of the two sentences this shows is a key the view model picks, the way the recommendation
        reasons travel, so the words follow the chosen language. It said the same thing either way
        until 2026-08-21, while holding the service that knew: AnimationsEnabled is the negation of the
        reduced-motion preference.
      -->
      <Border
          x:Name="ReducedMotionSurface"
          Padding="16"
          Background="{DynamicResource AccentSubtleBrush}"
          BorderBrush="{DynamicResource ShellHairlineBrush}"
          BorderThickness="1"
          CornerRadius="{DynamicResource CornerRadiusMedium}">
        <TextBlock
            Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimaryBrush}"
            Text="{Binding ReducedMotionNoticeKey, Converter={StaticResource AppearanceResourceKey}}"
            TextWrapping="Wrap" />
      </Border>
    </StackPanel>
  </Border>
</UserControl>
